.Dd October 3, 2026
.Dt MAILCRIER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mailcrier ,
.Nm sendmail ,
.Nm newaliases ,
.Nm mailq
.Nd deliver the mail of system tools to chat and webhook services
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl tiIv
.Op Fl f Ar sender
.Op Fl F Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar option
.Op Fl b Ar mode
.Op Fl q Ns Op Ar interval
.Op Fl -config Ar path
.Op Fl -
.Op Ar recipient ...
.Nm
.Fl -version | -help | -status | -check-config
.Nm
.Fl -probe
.Op Fl - Ar target ...
.Nm newaliases
.Nm mailq
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads one message on standard input and delivers it to the targets of
.Pa /etc/mailcrier.conf .
It is installed as
.Pa /usr/sbin/sendmail
and accepts the command lines of cron, at, sudo, mdadm, mailx and similar
callers.
.Pp
Flags follow
.Xr getopt 3 :
a value is glued
.Pq Fl froot
or the next argument
.Pq Fl f Ar root ,
flags without a value group
.Pq Fl ti ,
and
.Fl -
ends the options.
Options and recipients may come in any order before
.Fl - .
The value of a flag is never read as an option.
An unknown flag is logged and ignored.
.Pp
Recipients are the arguments, split at commas, and with
.Fl t
the addresses of the To, Cc and Bcc headers, without duplicates.
A message with a Resent-To, Resent-Cc or Resent-Bcc header, even an empty one,
is a resent message: then
.Fl t
takes the addresses of these three headers instead.
Bcc and Resent-Bcc headers are removed from the message.
.Pa /etc/aliases
and
.Pa .forward
are not read.
.Pp
The envelope sender is the value of
.Fl f
or
.Fl r ,
else the first Resent-From address, else the From address, else
.Ev EMAIL ,
else
.Ev USER
or
.Ev LOGNAME
at the host name, else the login name of the real user id at the host name.
When the setgid bit applies, the environment is skipped; a user id without an
entry in the user database gives an empty sender.
.Pp
The text of a notification is the text/plain part of the message, else its
text/html part converted to text; other parts are attachments.
The conversion collapses white space outside pre elements and reduces several
empty lines in a row to one everywhere, pre elements included.
Encoded words, quoted-printable and base64 are decoded and every charset is
converted to UTF-8.
A body declared US-ASCII, or in an unknown charset, that is valid UTF-8 is
taken as UTF-8.
Text without a charset or declared US-ASCII that is not valid UTF-8, and text
declared ISO-8859-1, is read as windows-1252.
.Pp
The message goes to its targets at the same time, to all of them unless
routes choose them, see
.Sx ROUTING ,
each in the markup of its service, or as it is to a program.
A text longer than a target accepts is cut, counted the way the service counts
it: a subject longer than a quarter of the limit is cut at a word and ends
with
.Dq ... ,
then the list of attachments and then the body, which ends with a notice.
When the rest of the text alone is too long, the text is cut hard, for
Telegram between tags and entities with the open tags closed.
An attachment the target sends files but not this one, over its size or number
of files, stays in the list with a notice.
.Pp
With the default
.Ic on_long No = Qq file
of a target that sends files, a cut text is followed by the full text as
.Pa message.txt ,
the first file of the message, or with
.Ic long_file No = Qq eml
by the message itself without its Bcc fields as
.Pa message.eml .
.Ic on_long No = Qq truncate ,
or a target without files, ends the cut body with the size of the full text
instead;
.Qq blockquote
is
.Qq file
with the cut body in an expandable blockquote in Telegram.
.Ic max_text
replaces the limit of the service and
.Ic max_lines
cuts the body after that many lines.
A target that rejects the text with 400, as Telegram does with markup it cannot
parse, gets the full text once more as a file alone.
.Pp
.Ic template ,
a Go text/template, or
.Ic template_file ,
the absolute path of a file holding one, replaces the built-in template of a
target of any type but
.Cm exec .
It writes the markup of the target, Telegram HTML for
.Cm telegram
and the JSON body for
.Cm http ,
and escapes what comes from the message with
.Ic tgHTML ,
.Ic discordEscape ,
.Ic slackEscape ,
.Ic mmEscape ,
.Ic toJson
and the like.
Besides the functions of text/template it has
.Ic toUpper ,
.Ic toLower ,
.Ic trimSpace ,
.Ic trimEnd ,
.Ic title ,
.Ic default ,
.Ic join ,
.Ic match ,
.Ic reReplaceAll ,
.Ic tz ,
.Ic date ,
.Ic lines ,
.Ic head ,
.Ic tail ,
.Ic truncate ,
.Ic indent ,
.Ic pathSegment
and
.Ic humanizeBytes .
A template that does not parse, or uses define, template or block, is a
configuration error.
The renderings of the text of one message for one target may take 2 s
together, ending no later than
.Ic deadline ,
each one 1 s and 1 MiB of output.
A template that fails while rendering a message, past either limit, with an
error of a function or with nothing but white space, leaves that message the
built-in template, as does a 400 to its text, once; the log records
.Dq template failed, built-in used .
A template that ran out of time stays failed for the rest of the process.
A path, query or header template has no built-in one: when it fails, the
target fails permanently for that message, logged as
.Dq request template failed, message not sent .
.Sh TARGETS
Each
.Li "[target.NAME]"
table of the configuration is one target; its
.Ic type
selects the service:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm telegram
Bot API
.Cm sendMessage
in the HTML parse mode, text of at most 4096 characters after entities, an
emoji counted once, and one
.Cm sendDocument
per attachment, up to 10 files of 50 MB; a text of at most 1024 characters
goes as the caption of the first document instead.
.It Cm discord
One webhook execution with wait=true and no mention allowed, text of at most
2000 characters, up to 10 files of 20 MiB and 25 MiB together.
.It Cm slack
Web API
.Cm chat.postMessage
with the bot token, text of at most 40000 characters, and up to 10 files
shared in the thread of the message.
.It Cm ntfy
A JSON publish with the subject as title, text of at most 4096 bytes, and one
more message per attachment, up to 10 files of 15 MiB.
.It Cm http
One POST, or PUT or PATCH with
.Ic method ,
of the JSON document of its preset,
.Cm mattermost ,
.Cm slack-webhook
or
.Cm generic-json ,
or of its
.Ic template ;
extra headers override the Content-Type.
Host, Content-Length, Transfer-Encoding and Trailer are set by the HTTP
client and rejected as headers,
and so are Connection, Keep-Alive, Proxy-Connection and Upgrade,
which HTTP/2 does not carry.
A GET carries no body and takes none of
.Ic preset ,
.Ic template ,
.Ic template_file ,
.Ic max_text
and
.Ic max_lines .
.Ic path
is appended to the path of
.Ic url
and the values of the
.Ic query
table to its query; they and the header values are templates.
Scheme, host and port come from
.Ic url
alone: a path that renders empty appends nothing, and a rendered path that
does not start with a single slash, or holds
.Dq ? ,
.Dq # ,
a backslash, a control character or a dot segment, and a rendered header
value with a line break or NUL, fail the target permanently before any
request; what
.Ic path
writes before its first action is checked so when the configuration is
loaded.
Only
.Cm slack-webhook
is cut, to 40000 characters, unless
.Ic max_text
sets a limit.
.It Cm exec
Runs the program of
.Ic argv ,
an array whose first element is an absolute path, without a shell.
Its stdin is the message without its Bcc and Resent-Bcc fields; its
environment holds only
.Ev PATH ,
.Ev LANG Ns = Ns Li C.UTF-8 ,
.Ev TZ
when set, and
.Ev MAILCRIER_SUBJECT ,
.Ev MAILCRIER_FROM ,
.Ev MAILCRIER_TO
(the recipients without blind copies),
.Ev MAILCRIER_HOSTNAME ,
.Ev MAILCRIER_TARGET ,
.Ev MAILCRIER_MSGID
and
.Ev MAILCRIER_SIZE ,
each with line breaks and NUL turned into spaces and cut to 4096 bytes.
Exit status 0 is a delivery, 75 a temporary failure, anything else a
permanent one.
Past
.Ic timeout ,
30 s by default, or the deadline, the process group of the program is
killed and the failure is temporary; so it is after SIGINT, SIGTERM or SIGHUP
to
.Nm
once the message is read, while before that such a signal discards the
message.
A setgid call runs the program with the real user and group ids of the
caller; a queue run as the mailcrier user runs it with the mailcrier group.
.Ic argv
is visible to all local users and holds no secret; a secret the program reads
itself is readable by every caller of a setgid call.
Its stdout and stderr, up to 4096 bytes, are logged.
.It Cm shoutrrr
The plain text through the service of the shoutrrr library that the scheme of
.Ic url
selects, without files; an unknown scheme, a URL the service rejects or a
matrix URL with a user name instead of an access token is a configuration
error.
A failure after an HTTP answer is classified by its status, any other failure
is temporary.
A binary built with the noshoutrrr tag rejects the target as a configuration
error.
.El
.Pp
.Ic max_file_size
replaces the size limit of one file, in bytes, for every type but
.Cm http ,
.Cm exec
and
.Cm shoutrrr ;
a bigger file is listed as not sent.
.Pp
429 and 5xx answers, and any answer with a Retry-After header, are temporary
failures; other rejections are permanent.
A target that took the text but not all files counts as delivered.
.Sh ROUTING
Without a
.Li "[[route]]"
table every target gets every message, except one whose recipients are all
direct chats, which goes to those chats alone.
With routes, the rules are checked from the first for each recipient on its
own: the targets of the first rule whose conditions all match are taken, and
.Ic continue No = Li true
goes on to add those of the next matching rules.
The targets of all recipients are joined.
A rule without conditions matches every message;
.Ic targets ,
a list of configured target names, is required.
.Pp
The conditions are
.Ic subject ,
the decoded subject;
.Ic sender ,
the envelope sender;
and
.Ic recipient ,
one envelope recipient, Bcc included, as its address without the display
name; a local name such as
.Li root
has no domain.
Each is a glob, matching the whole value with case ignored, where
.Li *
is any run of characters,
.Li \&?
one character and a backslash makes the next character literal; or, under
the key with
.Li _regex ,
an RE2 expression that matches anywhere unless anchored, with case as
written.
A message without recipients matches only rules without
.Ic recipient .
.Pp
When no rule matches and no recipient is a direct chat, the message is held
in
.Pa hold/
with the reason
.Dq no route
and the call exits 64; with the spool off it is lost.
A queue run routes it again with the rules of the moment, until
.Ic hold_ttl
moves it to
.Pa failed/ ;
every call of the same user and every
.Fl q
read it again first, out of the budget of their queue run.
The targets of a queued message are fixed when it is queued.
.Pp
A
.Li "[[suppress]]"
rule takes
.Ic subject
and
.Ic sender
conditions, at least one; a message that matches one of these rules is
neither sent nor spooled, logged as
.Dq message suppressed ,
and the call exits 0.
.Pp
With
.Ic telegram_direct
in
.Li "[general]"
naming a telegram target, a recipient
.Ar chat Ns @telegram
gets a copy of that target sent to
.Ar chat ,
a numeric id or an @username, without its
.Ic message_thread_id .
Only the chats of
.Ic telegram_direct_chats
get a copy, at most
.Ic telegram_direct_max ,
10 by default, per message; other addresses of the domain are ordinary
recipients and logged as a warning.
Direct recipients are not routed.
A negative id goes after
.Fl -
on the command line.
.Sh QUEUE
Before the delivery the message is written to the spool,
.Pa /var/spool/mailcrier
unless
.Ic dir
of the
.Li "[spool]"
table names another directory or is empty, which turns the spool off.
The entry keeps the raw message and the state of each target; it is removed
once every target has the message or has rejected it.
When a target failed by a panic, an internal error, the entry moves to
.Pa failed/
with the reason
.Dq internal error
instead, once no other target waits for it: a retry would repeat the error.
A panic on one entry of a queue run moves that entry to
.Pa failed/
with the same reason and the run goes on;
.Fl q
then exits 70, the queue run after a call does not change its exit status.
A panic of a call after its message is read and before the message is in
the spool holds it in
.Pa hold/
with the reason
.Dq internal error ;
the call exits 70 and runs no queue.
A target that fails temporarily is tried again by a later queue run, one
minute after the first failure, twice as long after each further failure, at
most after 24 hours and never before the Retry-After of the service; later
entries skip a target that asked for a delay until it ends.
An entry older than 7 days moves to
.Pa failed/ ,
which keeps it 30 days; for a message that was held the 7 days count from
its release.
An entry whose state file cannot be read is left alone, and
.Fl q
exits 74; when the file is corrupt, the entry moves to
.Pa failed/
with the reason
.Dq corrupt sidecar
once its message file is older than the same limit, counted from the time
the file was written.
A retry renders the message with the configuration of the moment, to the
targets fixed when it was queued; a target no longer configured fails for it.
Delivery is at least once: a process killed after a service accepted the
message, a timeout after that, or a power failure repeats the delivery.
.Pp
A message whose configuration is rejected is kept in
.Pa hold/ ,
in the default spool when the file cannot be read at all; the next queue run
with a valid configuration routes it as a new message, and
.Fl q
moves it from the default spool when the valid file names another
.Ic dir .
.Pp
A call runs the queue briefly after its own message: the caller's entries
only, at most 20 of them within 10 seconds, skipped when another call of the
same user runs it.
.Fl q
runs it for up to 60 seconds: all entries for root, the
.Li mailcrier
user and a caller without the setgid bit, the caller's own entries for
everyone else.
An entry another process is working on is skipped.
The packages run
.Fl q
as
.Li mailcrier
every 5 minutes, by a systemd timer or by cron.
.Pp
The spool holds at most 1000 messages and 256 MiB, and 200 messages and
64 MiB per user; users other than root and
.Li mailcrier
fill at most 80% of the totals.
A message over a limit is delivered without an entry.
The spool must be on a local file system: the locks do not work over NFS.
Missing areas are created in an existing directory; with the setgid bit the
packages create them, owned by root and the
.Li mailcrier
group, mode 2770.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration is a TOML file, parsed strictly on every call: an unknown
key, a key that the type of its target does not use, or an invalid value
rejects the whole file, and the call exits 78.
Errors name the file, line and column and never quote a value.
A duration is a Go duration such as
.Li \&"15s"
or
.Li \&"168h" ;
every duration and limit must be positive.
.Pp
The
.Li "[general]"
table:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic syslog_tag
The tag of every syslog record;
.Li mailcrier
by default.
.It Ic http_timeout
Bound of one HTTP request, from dialing to the end of the response body;
15 s by default.
.It Ic deadline
Bound of the delivery of one message to all its targets; 30 s by default.
Reading stdin and the configuration is not under it.
.It Ic telegram_direct , Ic telegram_direct_chats , Ic telegram_direct_max
The telegram target whose copies go to direct chats, the chats allowed, as
integers and @usernames, and the most copies per message, 10 by default;
see
.Sx ROUTING .
.El
.Pp
The
.Li "[spool]"
table:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic dir
The spool directory, an absolute path;
.Pa /var/spool/mailcrier
by default, and the empty string turns the spool off.
.It Ic drain_budget , Ic drain_max_messages
Bound of the queue run after the own message of a call: 10 s and 20
entries by default.
.It Ic run_budget
Bound of a queue run of
.Fl q ;
60 s by default.
.It Ic queue_ttl , Ic hold_ttl , Ic failed_ttl
Age after which an entry of
.Pa queue/
or
.Pa hold/
moves to
.Pa failed/ ,
7 days each by default, and time in
.Pa failed/
before it is deleted, 30 days.
.It Ic max_queue_messages , Ic max_queue_bytes
Limits of the whole spool: 1000 messages and 268435456 bytes (256 MiB) by
default.
.It Ic max_queue_messages_per_uid , Ic max_queue_bytes_per_uid
Limits of the entries of one user: 200 messages and 67108864 bytes
(64 MiB) by default.
.El
.Pp
The
.Li "[strings]"
table replaces the English notices written in place of missing content;
a key set must not be blank:
.Ic no_subject ,
.Ic empty_body ,
.Ic truncated ,
.Ic truncated_size
with one
.Li %s
for the size of the full text,
.Ic more_attachments
with one
.Li %d
for the number of attachments left out, and
.Ic not_sent .
.Ic truncated
without
.Ic truncated_size
stands for both.
.Pp
Each
.Li "[target.NAME]"
table is a target; NAME matches
.Li [a-z0-9-]+ .
Its keys, besides
.Ic type :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic token , Ic token_file
The token of
.Cm telegram
and
.Cm slack ,
or the absolute path of a file holding it; exactly one of the two.
.It Ic url , Ic url_file
The endpoint of
.Cm discord ,
.Cm ntfy ,
.Cm http
and
.Cm shoutrrr ,
or the absolute path of a file holding it; exactly one of the two.
An http or https URL, for
.Cm shoutrrr
any URL with a scheme.
The content of a file has its surrounding white space removed.
.It Ic chat_id , Ic message_thread_id , Ic disable_notification
The chat, an integer or a string, required, the forum topic and silent
sending of
.Cm telegram .
.It Ic channel
The channel of
.Cm slack ,
required, or of the
.Cm mattermost
preset of
.Cm http ,
which also takes
.Ic username .
.It Ic preset , Ic method , Ic headers , Ic path , Ic query
The body, the method, extra headers, the path and the query of
.Cm http ;
see
.Sx TARGETS .
.It Ic on_long , Ic long_file
What a text over the limit gets,
.Qq file
by default,
.Qq truncate
or
.Qq blockquote ,
and the file of the full text,
.Qq text
by default or
.Qq eml ;
not for
.Cm http ,
.Cm exec
and
.Cm shoutrrr .
.It Ic max_text , Ic max_lines , Ic max_file_size
The text limit in the unit of the service, the lines of the body, and the
size of one file in bytes.
.It Ic argv , Ic timeout
The command line of
.Cm exec ,
required, and the bound of one run, 30 s by default.
.It Ic template , Ic template_file
A template replacing the built-in one, or the absolute path of a file
holding it; not for
.Cm exec .
.El
.Pp
A
.Li "[[route]]"
table takes
.Ic subject ,
.Ic subject_regex ,
.Ic sender ,
.Ic sender_regex ,
.Ic recipient ,
.Ic recipient_regex ,
.Ic targets
and
.Ic continue ;
a
.Li "[[suppress]]"
table the subject and sender conditions; see
.Sx ROUTING .
.Pp
.Fl -check-config
reports the errors and warnings of a file without sending anything.
.Sh SECURITY
The intended install is setgid: the binary
.Li root:mailcrier
mode 2755, the configuration and its
.Ic token_file ,
.Ic url_file
and
.Ic template_file
files
.Li root:mailcrier
mode 0640, so that the jobs of any user can send while only root and the
binary read the secrets.
The spool directory and its areas are
.Li root:mailcrier
mode 2770; entries are created with mode 0660 under the umask 007.
.Pp
When the setgid bit gives a user other than root the group, the process
first executes itself once more with the environment reduced to
.Ev USER ,
.Ev LOGNAME ,
.Ev HOME ,
.Ev LANG ,
.Ev LC_*
and a zone name in
.Ev TZ ;
if that fails it replaces its environment the same way, speaks HTTP/1.1
only and logs
.Dq reexec failed .
.Fl -config
and
.Ev MAILCRIER_CONFIG
are ignored with a warning, and
.Fl -check-config
and
.Fl -probe
exit 64 when given them, and 77 for everyone but the mailcrier user.
An
.Cm exec
program runs with the real user and group ids of the caller.
.Pp
Tokens, URLs and the literal text of header, query and path templates are
masked as
.Li ***
in everything logged, and configuration errors never quote a value.
Without the setgid bit, as in a container, the process runs with the ids
of its caller, who must be able to read the configuration.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar sender , Fl r Ar sender
Envelope sender, angle brackets around it removed; an empty value or
.Li <>
is the null sender.
Without a value or with a line break the call exits 64.
.It Fl F Ar name
Full name of the sender; a line break exits 64.
.It Fl t
Take recipients from the To, Cc and Bcc headers as well, or only from the
Resent-To, Resent-Cc and Resent-Bcc headers when the message has any of them.
.It Fl i , Fl oi
A line with a single dot is ordinary text.
Without it such a line ends the message, and the first dot of a line
starting with two dots is removed.
.It Fl o Ar option
Ignored, except
.Fl oi .
.It Fl b Ar mode
The first letter decides:
.Cm m
delivers, the default;
.Cm i
does nothing;
.Cm p
lists the queue;
.Cm s
is refused with exit status 64; other modes are ignored with a warning.
.It Fl q Ns Op Ar interval
Runs the queue once, see
.Sx QUEUE ;
the interval is ignored.
.It Fl I
Does nothing, like
.Fl bi .
.It Fl C Ar file
Ignored with a warning.
.It Fl B , Fl h , Fl L , Fl N , Fl O , Fl R , Fl V , Fl X , Fl p , Fl A
Take a value and are ignored.
.It Fl d , Fl e
Ignored; the value is glued or the next argument unless it starts with a
dash.
.It Fl v , Fl m , Fl n , Fl U , Fl G
Ignored.
.It Fl -config Ar path
Read another configuration file; ignored with a warning when the setgid
bit of the binary applies to a caller other than root.
.It Fl -version
Print the version.
.It Fl -help
Print the modes, flags, configuration files and exit statuses.
.It Fl -status
Print the numbers of queued, held and failed messages, the files in
.Pa tmp/ ,
the bytes of the spool and the age of the oldest entry as one logfmt line.
.It Fl -check-config
Check the configuration and send nothing: load it and build its targets as
a call does, which stops at the first error, then warn about
a secret file or a configuration with secrets readable by all users,
a file or a directory on the way to it that the group of the binary cannot
read (these only when the setgid bit applies, root included),
a shoutrrr URL of a service with a target type of its own,
the
.Cm slack-webhook
preset on a Discord host,
routes without a rule without conditions,
a target that no route names,
an
.Cm exec
program that is not executable,
and a template that fails on a built-in sample message.
The sample has no attachments, HTML, long text or Bcc; access control lists
are not seen.
Errors and warnings go to standard error, one per line, followed by a line
with their numbers; standard output stays empty, and stdin and the spool are
not read.
Takes no arguments.
.It Fl -probe Op Fl - Ar target ...
Send a sample message, subject
.Dq mailcrier probe from Ar host ,
to every target, or to the targets named after
.Fl - ;
an unknown name exits 64 before anything is sent.
These are real notifications and hooks run; routes, suppress rules and
direct chats do not apply, and stdin, the spool and the queue are not
touched.
Prints one logfmt line per target to standard output, such as
.Li target=mm class=temp status=503 err="..." ,
with
.Li template=fallback
when the built-in template stood in for a failed one.
Exits 0 when every target took the message, 69 when one rejected it, 75
when one failed temporarily and none rejected it.
.El
.Pp
Of several mode options the last one wins.
.Pp
Called as
.Nm newaliases
the program does nothing; called as
.Nm mailq ,
or with
.Fl bp ,
it lists the queue: every entry with the state of each target for root, the
.Li mailcrier
user and a caller without the setgid bit, the numbers alone for everyone
else; a spool directory that does not exist lists as empty.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev MAILCRIER_CONFIG
Another configuration file, like
.Fl -config .
.It Ev EMAIL , Ev USER , Ev LOGNAME
Sender of a message without
.Fl f
and without a Resent-From or From header; ignored when the setgid bit
applies.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/sbin/mailcrier
The binary;
.Pa /usr/sbin/sendmail ,
.Pa /usr/lib/sendmail ,
.Pa /usr/bin/newaliases
and
.Pa /usr/bin/mailq
are links to it.
.It Pa /etc/mailcrier.conf
The configuration.
.It Pa /etc/mailcrier.d/
Files of
.Ic token_file ,
.Ic url_file
and
.Ic template_file ,
by convention; any absolute path works.
.It Pa /usr/share/doc/mailcrier/examples/
Example configurations: a reference of every table with one target of each
type, and files for single scenarios such as routes, templates or a
container.
.It Pa mailcrier-queue.service , Pa mailcrier-queue.timer
The systemd units that run
.Fl q
as
.Li mailcrier
every 5 minutes.
.It Pa /etc/cron.d/mailcrier , Pa /etc/crontabs/mailcrier
The same queue run by cron where systemd is not running and the binary is
installed, the second on Alpine.
.It Pa /var/spool/mailcrier/queue/ , Pa hold/ , Pa failed/
Entries: the message and its state beside it.
.It Pa /var/spool/mailcrier/tmp/
Files being written; a queue run removes those older than one hour.
.It Pa /var/spool/mailcrier/locks/
Queue run locks, one per user; removal of the package deletes them when
the spool holds no message.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
A target accepted the message, even if another rejected it; or none
rejected it and it is queued for those that failed temporarily; or a
suppress rule matched; or a mode without a message succeeded, which for
.Fl -check-config
means no error, warnings aside, and for
.Fl -probe
that every target was reached.
.It 64
Usage error: a sender flag without a value, a line break in an address
or in the full name,
.Fl bs ,
.Fl -check-config
with an argument,
.Fl -probe
naming a target that is not configured, or either with
.Fl -config
or
.Ev MAILCRIER_CONFIG
from a caller the setgid bit applies to; or no route selects a target, and
the message is held or lost with the spool off.
.It 66
Standard input cannot be read.
.It 69
No target accepted the message: one rejected it, or all failed temporarily
with the spool off.
.Fl -probe :
a target rejected the sample message.
.It 70
Internal error, a panic: of the call, or on an entry of the queue run of
.Fl q .
.It 73
A target failed temporarily, or a message to be held could not be held,
and the spool entry could not be created: the directory is missing or not
writable, or a limit is reached.
.It 74
A target failed temporarily, or a message to be held could not be held,
and the spool entry could not be written,
.Fl q
could not read the spool,
.Fl q
or
.Fl -status
found it not writable,
.Fl -status
found no spool directory, or
.Nm mailq
or
.Fl -status
could not write their output.
.It 75
Only
.Fl -probe :
a target failed temporarily and none rejected the sample message; nothing
is queued.
.It 77
A service mode requested by a caller without the right to it.
.It 78
The configuration cannot be read or is invalid; a message is held, or
lost with the spool off.
.Fl -check-config
found an error, or
.Fl -probe
cannot use the configuration; nothing is held.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A minimal configuration that sends to one Telegram chat, with the token in
a file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[target.ops-telegram]
type = "telegram"
token_file = "/etc/mailcrier.d/tg.token"
chat_id = -1001234567890
.Ed
.Pp
Check it, then send a test message to that target alone:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# mailcrier --check-config
/etc/mailcrier.conf: 0 errors, 0 warnings
# mailcrier --probe -- ops-telegram
target=ops-telegram class=ok
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr cron 8
